From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shrek Shao <shrekshao@google.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:52:50 -0700
Subject: [gl] Use blit for unsupported glReadPixels formats pt 1

Under OpenGL ES, glReadPixels only guarantees a limited
set of format/type combinations. Mostly format = GL_RGBA.
Reading formats like R8Unorm, RG8Unorm with native format/type pair
with glReadPixels is not guaranteed to succeed.

This CL add toggles to emulate these copies with compute blits, for
formats with existing blit implementation:
- UseBlitForNonRGBAUnormTextureToBufferCopy
- UseBlitForNonRGBAFloatTextureToBufferCopy

Enable these toggles by default on the OpenGLES backend.

Bug: 556959073
Change-Id: Idc24c5736bbacc9176d34920946055b9ba332625
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/340475
Commit-Queue: Shrek Shao <shrekshao@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
M150 Dawn still derives isFloat32Renderable/isFloat16Renderable/isRG11B10UfloatRenderable from GL_EXT_color_buffer_float and has no VulkanSplitBufferTextureCopyForArrayLayers toggle. The two new toggles and the OpenGL ES defaults block were added; the existing renderable-based defaults for RG11B10Ufloat/Float16/Float32 were kept instead of upstream's DAWN_CHECK plus unconditional false defaults (upstream's temporary RG11B10Ufloat=false is superseded by part 3 of this series).

